positions we have taken or expect to take in a tax return, we apply a more likely than not threshold (that is, a likelihood of more than 50 percent), under which we must conclude a tax position is more likely than not to be sustained, assuming that the position will be examined by the appropriate taxing authority that has full knowledge of all relevant information, to recognize the benefit. In determining our provision for income taxes, we use judgment, reflecting our estimates and assumptions, in applying the more likely than not threshold. We recognize accrued interest and penalties for our unrecognized tax benefits as a component of tax expense. </ix:continuation>","relative_character_range":[2178,2913],"root_raw_xml_sha256":"dd37614bbf3c0f5d278313984e903aa33ca8ac87128f58eedeccc2ff2a858912","source_index":24}],"reason":null,"request":{"anchor":{"kind":"NATIVE_FACT","source_index":418,"unit_id":"sha256:3345ce064f9231ae17b6b0133c01f16d4bc21ed1866bd7c9e1bf22fa7760d5b9"},"target":{"element_id":"f-408-1","kind":"XML_ELEMENT_ID"}},"status":"LOCATED"},{"context":[{"element_id":"f-408-2","kind":"NATIVE_SUPPLEMENT","original_element":{"attributes":{"id":"f-408-2"},"end_character":1352321,"local_name":"continuation","namespace":"http://www.xbrl.org/2013/inlineXBRL","namespace_environment_id":"sha256:2063b97c2889de88d2c8e0474ee1aeaabd277301b092cfc8b232678f06a6d87c","namespaces":{"":"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml","country":"http://xbrl.sec.gov/country/2025","cyd":"http://xbrl.sec.gov/cyd/2025","dei":"http://xbrl.sec.gov/dei/2025","ecd":"http://xbrl.sec.gov/ecd/2025","iso4217":"http://www.xbrl.org/2003/iso4217","ix":"http://www.xbrl.org/2013/inlineXBRL","ixt":"http://www.xbrl.org/inlineXBRL/transformation/2020-02-12","ixt-sec":"http://www.sec.gov/inlineXBRL/transformation/2015-08-31","link":"http://www.xbrl.org/2003/linkbase","mar":"http://www.marriott.com/20251231","srt":"http://fasb.org/srt/2025","us-gaap":"http://fasb.org/us-gaap/2025","xbrldi":"http://xbrl.org/2006/xbrldi","xbrli":"http://www.xbrl.org/2003/instance","xlink":"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink","xsi":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"},"raw_xml_sha256":"7c8f607e986d1e9866d707e06128bffd93b533f9bac6f6235548fa2c46afd568","relative_end_character":1380,"relative_start_character":244,"start_character":1351185},"original_unit_id":"sha256:4af0523b4e303de27c96f37785073b9f027b973ede4855205d487cea14f7087b","raw_xml":"<ix:continuation id=\"f-408-2\"><div style=\"margin-top:9pt;text-indent:22.5pt\"><span style=\"color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%\">Deferred income tax balances reflect the effects of temporary differences between the carrying amounts of assets and liabilities and their tax bases, as well as from net operating loss and tax credit carry-forwards. We state those balances at the enacted tax rates we expect will be in effect when we pay or recover the taxes. Deferred income tax assets represent amounts available to reduce income taxes we will pay on taxable income in future years. We evaluate our ability to realize these future tax deductions and credits by assessing whether we expect to have sufficient future taxable income from all sources, including reversal of taxable temporary differences, forecasted operating earnings, and available tax planning strategies to utilize these future deductions and credits. We establish a valuation allowance when we no longer consider it more likely than not that a deferred tax asset will be realized.</span></div></ix:continuation>","relative_character_range":[244,1380],"root_raw_xml_sha256":"9c3f078ed7331027c5ac51d7344a533790b913459f84e81e4799fbfacb597503","source_index":3}],"reason":null,"request":{"anchor":{"kind":"NATIVE_FACT","source_index":418,"unit_id":"sha256:3345ce064f9231ae17b6b0133c01f16d4bc21ed1866bd7c9e1bf22fa7760d5b9"},"target":{"element_id":"f-408-2","kind":"XML_ELEMENT_ID"}},"status":"LOCATED"}],"semantic_acceptance":false,"source_id":"sha256:f49af1b29c